class:: HarmonicChange
summary:: Causal tonal-centroid change magnitude
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Tonal
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/HPCP, Classes/HarmonicPeaks

description::
Applies the Harte, Sandler and Gasser (2006) tonal-centroid transform and computes Euclidean distance between the current centroid and the centroid two accepted observations earlier. This is the centred harmonic-change difference reported one observation late, after optional causal exponential smoothing. The first two observations output zero. Values occur on accepted trigger blocks; other blocks output zero. Tonal-centroid distance detects changes in pitch-class geometry and can also respond to changing timbre or noise.



classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: chroma
A C-first Array of 12, 24, 36, or 120 nonnegative pitch-class values. Higher resolutions fold to nearest semitones where a twelve-class representation is required.

argument:: smooth
Causal exponential smoothing time in seconds, zero disables. Time follows the actual interval between trigger updates.

argument:: trig
A positive value processes this control block. For FFT-derived features pass chain >= 0 so each analysis frame is used once; default 1 processes each control block.

returns::
Nonnegative six-dimensional Euclidean distance, delayed by one observation relative to the centred difference.

examples::
The analysis controls audible synthesis or processing. Boot the server first; use headphones or moderate speaker volume.
code::
(
Routine({
    var buffer = Buffer.read(s, ExampleFiles.child);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2TonalExample = {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, buffer, BufRateScale.kr(buffer), loop: 1);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);
        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(4096), source, 0.25);
        var chroma = HPCP.kr(chain, harmonics: 1);
        var change = HarmonicChange.kr(chroma, 0.05, chain >= 0);
        var hits = PinkNoise.ar(0.08) * Decay2.kr(change > 0.12, 0.001, 0.12);
        var sound = (source * 0.12 + hits) ! 2;
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;
    ~mir2TonalBuffer = buffer;
}).play(AppClock);
)
::

Stop and release:
code::
(
~mir2TonalExample.free;
~mir2TonalBuffer.free;
)
::

